          "create_time": 1792089030.178,
          "update_time": 1792089056.662,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "**Yes: there is a precise reformulation of RH involving the topology of compact surfaces with a natural real structure.** I derived and independently checked it. Its originality remains unestablished: it combines classical Jensen-polynomial theory with real algebraic geometry.\n\nDefine\n\\[\nf(z)=\\xi\\!\\left(\\tfrac12+\\sqrt z\\right)\n=\\sum_{k\\ge0}\\gamma_k\\frac{z^k}{k!},\n\\qquad\nJ_d(X)=\\sum_{k=0}^d\\binom dk\\gamma_kX^k.\n\\]\nThe first expression defines an entire function through its power series; the coefficients are explicit positive moments of your complete theta source.\n\nFor each \\(g\\ge1\\), let \\(C_g\\) be the smooth compact normalization of\n\\[\ny^2=J_{2g+1}(x).\n\\]\nThen\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\mathrm{RH}\\iff\nC_g(\\mathbb R)\\text{ has exactly }g+1\n\\text{ connected components for every }g\\ge1.}\n\\]\n\nThese components are disjoint circles fixed by complex conjugation. Equivalently, each specified surface has genus \\(g\\), and those circles divide it into two spheres with \\(g+1\\) holes.\n\nThe proof handles possible repeated polynomial roots through normalization. It also proves the necessary strict Jensen hyperbolicity under RH **without assuming that zeta zeros are simple**. The reverse implication follows from the real-component count and convergence of the scaled Jensen polynomials to \\(f\\). The classical foundations are described by [O’Sullivan](https://fsw01.bcc.cuny.edu/cormac.osullivan/Research/xi-revised.pdf) and [Gross–Harris](https://www.numdam.org/item/10.24033/asens.1401.pdf).\n\nI saved the full [compact-surface proof](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-2/active/22_theta_manifold_geometry/notes/01_physical_jet_geometry/05_JENSEN_HYPERELLIPTIC_TOPOLOGY_20261015.md).\n\nA second simplification fits the current manuscript more directly. Use the **single spacetime first jet**\n\\[\nJ(t,x)=(H(t,x),H_x(t,x)).\n\\]\nAt a collision of spatial multiplicity \\(m\\), its local topological index is\n\\[\n-\\left\\lfloor m/2\\right\\rfloor.\n\\]\nConsequently, for a compact spacetime domain with nonzero boundary jet,\n\\[\n\\operatorname{wind}_{\\partial D}(H+iH_x)\n=-\\sum_{\\text{interior collisions}}\\left\\lfloor m/2\\right\\rfloor,\n\\]\nusing orientation \\(dt\\wedge dx\\).\n\nEvery collision contributes with the same sign. **Zero boundary winding therefore excludes all interior collisions.** This handles both parity branches together and suggests a certificate requiring control only along the boundary, without computing an interior energy floor. Investigation 21 supplies the confinement and local splitting needed for the global RH connection.\n\nThe general winding mechanism already appears explicitly in [Angenent’s work, §3](https://people.math.wisc.edu/~angenent/preprints/extatic.pdf). Its potential contribution here would be a useful theta-specific boundary estimate or a demonstrably better certification method. The [spacetime note](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-2/active/22_theta_manifold_geometry/notes/01_physical_jet_geometry/04_SPACETIME_INDEX_AND_MARKED_TOPOLOGY_20261015.md) contains the proof and proposed test.\n\nMy assessment of the existing manuscript is that its scalar stationary reduction remains the strongest established simplification; the checked arguments held up. The continuation note correctly identifies the unresolved arithmetic trace estimate. Bare hyperkähler or calibrated-manifold topology does not supply it: a collision cusp remains intrinsically homeomorphic to a disk, and the projective Gauss map cancels the common vanishing factor. The useful topology retains the real involution, marked phase map, or embedding.\n\n**A reformulation can be publishable without proving RH, but this work does not yet establish publishable novelty.** I would develop the compact-surface equivalence as a concise, carefully attributed note, while pursuing boundary winding as the more practical continuation of Investigations 21–22.\n\nThe [full review](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-2/active/22_theta_manifold_geometry/reviews/13_GEOMETRIC_SIMPLIFICATION_AND_TOPOLOGICAL_RH_REVIEW_20261015.md) records the proofs, limitations, and next steps. The manuscript is unchanged; 60 exact polynomial control cases passed."
            ]
          },
