            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "I continued the **arithmetic investigation** and obtained an exact prime-sieving formulation:\n\\[\nD_p\\Phi(u)=p^{-1/2}\\Phi\\!\\left(u+\\tfrac12\\log p\\right)\n=\\sum_{p\\mid n}\\phi_n(u).\n\\]\nTogether with classical [Möbius inversion](https://dlmf.nist.gov/27.5.E7), this gives explicit remainder bounds and an arithmetic condition that distinguishes theta from the weighted-square collision controls.\n\nThe main finding is a **necessary cancellation**: after the heat transform, each shifted term includes a lower-interval correction. At positive heat time, the separate Möbius series diverge; their paired differences converge rapidly. Any useful signed estimate must preserve that pairing.\n\nI also checked three alternative multipliers. Their present forms either recover the unresolved boundary trace or lose essential cancellation. **The required scalar signed inequality remains open.**\n\nSaved:\n\n- [Prime dilation identities and complete boundary calculation](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-2/active/22_theta_manifold_geometry/notes/03_theta_bundles_and_connections/11_MULTIPLICATIVE_DILATION_AND_COMPLETE_HEAT_PACKETS_20261015.md)\n- [Nonlocal arithmetic multiplier audit](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-2/active/22_theta_manifold_geometry/notes/03_theta_bundles_and_connections/12_NONLOCAL_ARITHMETIC_MULTIPLIERS_AND_BOUNDARY_OBSTRUCTIONS_20261015.md)\n- [Continuation and next research criterion](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-2/active/22_theta_manifold_geometry/notes/00_research_coordination/12_ARITHMETIC_DILATION_AND_NONLOCAL_CONTINUATION_20261015.md)\n\nIndependent review checked the analytic arguments; all **47 finite algebra checks** passed independently."
